lifeos-nix patch f4-b — Hard-kill the ElevenLabs cloud-TTS egress (keep local seam)

PROBLEM
  Three files reach api.elevenlabs.io for cloud text-to-speech:
    - LIFEOS/PULSE/VoiceServer/voice.ts   generateSpeech()   POST /v1/text-to-speech/{id}
    - LIFEOS/PULSE/modules/telegram.ts    synthesizeDaVoice() POST /v1/text-to-speech/{id}
    - LIFEOS/TOOLS/Doctor.ts              voice probeNetwork() POST /v1/text-to-speech/{id}
  Klemen's cut (ISA F4 decision, 2026-08-02): the ElevenLabs HTTP call is removed so
  voice is dead REGARDLESS of whether a key is set — stronger than relying on the
  no-key-shipped default. Honors the point-1 invariant (egress ⊆ {Anthropic}).

FIX (surgical; url + fetch removed in each)
  - voice.ts generateSpeech(): throw before any URL/fetch. The generateSpeech seam is
    kept intact on purpose — a LOCAL engine (e.g. Piper) can be slotted in here to
    return an ArrayBuffer, and the local audio-player path (ffplay/mpg123/paplay/aplay)
    below is untouched. Only the cloud synth dies.
  - telegram.ts synthesizeDaVoice(): throw before any URL/fetch. sendVoiceSummary()
    already guards on ELEVENLABS_API_KEY and swallows failures at WARN → throw is inert
    on the default no-key path, load-bearing if a key is ever present.
  - Doctor.ts voice probeNetwork(): return not-OK without the POST. Cloud voice is
    Doctor-declined by default in this build, so the probe never needed to reach out.

SCOPE / CO-EXISTENCE
  Three files, one hunk each. Disjoint from f4-a (lifeos.ts) and f2 (DeployCore.ts).
  Re-cut of the v5.0 intent behind 0026/0027 against the 7.1.1 tree paths.

VERIFICATION
  `rg 'api\.elevenlabs\.io'` over the patched files returns no fetch call (comments
  only). Hunks generated via `diff -u`, never hand-counted.

